  'XdVT-SsP1rU': 'A forest-green original physics-test playground: one solid wooden crate is shown in a short falling trajectory above a flat floor, with a pale ghosted earlier position above and the fully opaque current crate below. A single downward motion arrow and a floor contact shadow communicate rigid-body movement. A nearby simple component tile labelled Rigidbody links by a neutral line to the crate. One tiny cat physics tester releases the crate from a raised test platform using a lever; the crate stays undeformed. Pale-sage walls and white measuring grid without numbers. No soft-body distortion, force equation, mass or speed values, exaggerated bounce guarantee, detailed Unity editor screenshot or unsupported exact implementation. Focus on a rigid object with a physics component, not a generic class inheritance diagram.',
  o54EeQntWco: 'An original coral-and-mint character animation stage dominated by one original small blue mechanical explorer character with no franchise resemblance. The current character has a clear raised-arm stepping pose; a subtle pale earlier-pose silhouette behind it shows the motion. A few simple connected joint markers INSIDE the opaque character and one small joint-chain inset communicate skeletal skinning without detached limbs. A clearly visible light fixture BEHIND and to the upper right creates a narrow bright rim only along the character silhouette edges; the whole body must not glow or become transparent. One tiny calico cat lighting technician adjusts the rear light from the far left. Neutral labels 림라이트 and 스키닝 only. This is an original concept illustration, not a reconstruction of the actual lesson output. No borrowed human/game character, fake editor UI, numerical lighting claims, incorrect front-only rim light or duplicated general rigging workshop.',
  ZC3ciJ3_CLo: 'An original charcoal optical test chamber with two large spheres, one matte red and one reflective silver, above a pale checker floor. A tiny cat optical technician at the far left aims a simple camera through a visible rectangular image plane; a few clean amber camera rays pass through distinct image-plane cells toward the spheres, with one clear reflected path from the silver sphere. At the chamber edge a compact unbranded GPU tile array labelled CUDA feeds parallel image tiles into one rendered sphere image. Rays and rendered objects dominate, not the cat. Warm red and orange accents. No laser weapon, performance multiplier, CUDA source code, physical equations, clock, company logo, RTX claim or alleged screenshot. This introduces a CUDA ray-tracing project, not a promise to finish it in a specific number of days.',
  ul1hUxWiWdw: 'A cutaway game-window engineering scaffold stays intact while a small cat mechanic physically unplugs and slides out only the old drawing module labelled Win32 렌더링. The window shell and its input/message-loop foundation remain standing. Next to the vacant rendering connector is a neutral new-library module ready to connect, labelled 새 렌더러. A single large curved replacement arrow goes from the removed drawing module toward the new module. Slate-blue architecture, amber old-module accent and pale-gray preserved base. Make removal and renderer replacement preparation visible; do NOT depict deleting all of Win32, destroying the game window, rebuilding the entire engine, a completed DirectX feature demo, actual API source code or an invented benchmark.',
